---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${siteConfig.title}`}
  description={`About ${siteConfig.title} — background, engineering interests, and technical focus.`}
>
  <section style="margin-top: 0.2rem;">
    <p>
      Hi, I'm <strong>{siteConfig.author.name}</strong> (online as{" "}
      <strong>{siteConfig.author.handle}</strong>). I am a software developer
      based in {siteConfig.author.location}.
    </p>
    <p>
      My path into computing didn't start with code—it started with taking apart
      computer hardware, troubleshooting broken operating systems, and wondering
      why computers freeze. That hands-on tinkering grew into a deeper curiosity
      about software: how operating systems manage resources, how network
      protocols communicate across machines, and how to write backend services
      that don't break under pressure.
    </p>
    <p>
      In engineering, I prefer <strong>simplicity over cleverness</strong>. I
      value mechanical sympathy, deterministic behavior, and readable code. I'd
      rather understand a single system deeply than glue together five heavy
      frameworks I don't understand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>What I Care About</h2>
    <p>
      Most of my technical curiosity revolves around backend systems and data
      consistency:
    </p>
    <p>
      I spend a lot of time thinking about <strong>concurrency control</strong
      >—how to prevent race conditions and duplicate executions in distributed
      environments using techniques like Redis Redlock and database pessimistic
      locking. I'm fascinated by transactional resilience patterns, such as the
      Transactional Outbox pattern for reliable message delivery and idempotent
      API design.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beyond backend services, I do all my daily work in a minimal <strong
        >Arch Linux</strong
      > environment. Working close to the command line has taught me to appreciate
      small, single-purpose Unix tools, fast feedback loops, and efficient workflows.
      I also experiment with systems programming in <strong>Go</strong> to build lightweight
      CLI utilities.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Background & Life</h2>
    <p>
      I am currently studying Information Technology at Cao Thang Technical
      College. When I'm not writing code or debugging database queries, I enjoy
      practicing calisthenics, refining my terminal setup, and reading technical
      postmortems and system design notes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
    <p>
      I'm always happy to talk about backend systems, Linux tooling, or software
      craftsmanship. You can reach me directly:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email:</strong>{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.author.email}`}
          >{siteConfig.author.email}</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub:</strong>{" "}
        <a href={siteConfig.author.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >{siteConfig.author.github.replace("https://", "")}</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>LinkedIn:</strong>{" "}
        <a href={siteConfig.author.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >{siteConfig.author.linkedin.replace("https://", "")}</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
